---

<SimpleLayout
  title="Jakub Polec"
  description="Jakub Polec is a portfolio manager, quant systems architect, founder of QuantJourney, and builder of OneBook."
  canonical="https://jakubpolec.com/"
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <figure class="hero-image-wrap animate-in">
        <img
          src="/jpbg.jpeg"
          alt="Jakub Polec with Bill Gates during his Microsoft years"
          class="hero-image"
          width="440"
          height="550"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>With Bill Gates, during my Microsoft years.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 id="hero-title" class="animate-in">Jakub Polec</h1>
        <p class="role animate-in">Portfolio Manager &amp; Quant Systems Architect</p>
        <p class="lead animate-in">
          I invest proprietary capital and build research, portfolio, risk, and
          AI infrastructure for decisions that must remain explainable,
          reproducible, and operationally sound.
        </p>

        <p class="hero-proof animate-in">
          CERN <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Microsoft
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Oracle
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Quant Research
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> IBOR/PMS
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Risk Infrastructure
        </p>

        <div class="action-row hero-actions animate-in" aria-label="Contact links">
          <a
            href="https://calendly.com/jpolec/30min"
            class="button primary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >
            Set up a meeting
          </a>
          <a href="mailto:jakub@quantjourney.pro" class="button primary">
            Email me
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://linkedin.com/in/jakubpolec"
            class="button primary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >
            LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section animate-in" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="about-title">About</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section-copy">
        <p>
          I live in Dubai, UAE, and I am the founder of QuantJourney. I’m also a
          dad to three wonderful kids.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work sits between portfolio management, quantitative research, and
          technology. I manage a research-driven proprietary portfolio and build
          tools for people who need to make better decisions with imperfect
          information.
        </p>
        <p>
          My background is a slightly unusual mix of physics, technology,
          business, and financial markets. I have worked with Microsoft, Oracle,
          Orange, T-Mobile, hedge funds, proprietary trading firms,
          organisations across the Middle East, and research teams connected to
          CERN.
        </p>
        <p>
          I have led international teams and served as Head of Innovation for
          the MEA region, built three award-winning startups, and received two
          global marketing innovation awards from Microsoft’s CEO.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section animate-in" aria-labelledby="working-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="working-title">What I am working on</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section-copy item-stack">
        <article class="text-item">
          <h3>QuantJourney</h3>
          <p>
            QuantJourney is a research and investment technology platform
            connecting financial data, quantitative research, backtesting,
            portfolio analytics, risk, and AI workflows.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is built around a simple principle: every important result should
            be reproducible, explainable, and traceable back to its data,
            assumptions, model, and execution context.
          </p>
          <div class="project-links" aria-label="QuantJourney links">
            <a
              href="https://backtester.quantjourney.cloud"
              class="project-link"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              Backtester <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="https://api.quantjourney.cloud"
              class="project-link"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              Quant API <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="https://quantjourney.substack.com"
              class="project-link"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              Quant Blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/ecosystem" class="project-link">
              Explore ecosystem <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="text-item">
          <h3>OneBook</h3>
          <p>
            OneBook is institutional buy-side investment infrastructure for
            asset managers, funds, hedge funds, family offices, and proprietary
            investment teams. It connects research and systematic signals with
            scenario analysis, IBOR/PMS portfolio state, risk and constraints,
            approvals, and OMS order workflows.
          </p>
          <p>
            Rather than replacing existing systems of record, it provides a
            governed decision layer across data, research, PMS, OMS, risk, and
            execution — preserving point-in-time context, lineage, permissions,
            and outcomes from thesis and signal generation through post-trade
            review.
          </p>
          <div class="project-links" aria-label="OneBook link">
            <a
              href="https://quantjourney.cloud"
              class="project-link"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              Explore OneBook <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="text-item">
          <h3>Odysseus</h3>
          <p>
            Odysseus is a local-first control plane for coding agents, Git
            worktrees, and tmux sessions. It coordinates agent work through
            durable queues, isolated branches, review gates, and auditable
            evidence while keeping the terminal first-class.
          </p>
          <p>
            The goal is to make AI coding agents operationally useful: plan
            work before spending tokens, run parallel tasks safely, surface only
            the decisions that need human attention, and preserve enough context
            to review what happened.
          </p>
          <div class="project-links" aria-label="Odysseus link">
            <a
              href="https://github.com/jpolec/odysseus"
              class="project-link"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              View Odysseus on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

